    "finding": "The source model's sourcedAnimationCount counts fixed updates even when sourcedValue5 supplies a measured clock. The host counter accumulates the scaled timer delta."
  },
  "findings": [
    "The original draw trace hides earlier state differences: the first monitor raise finishes one update early in the model at 164, while the rebuild finishes at 165.",
    "At the first draw split, the rebuild animation counter is 11.3186 after update 1822 and reaches 12.374 only after update 1823. Its completion latch and BB entry therefore fire at 1824.",
    "Both experimental variants move BB entry to 1824 and match every draw count and RNG state through update 2047. A new draw discrepancy remains at 2048.",
    "This is independent of the effective BB AI cap, already observed as 15. It does not establish retail equivalence or identify the later disputed BB rolls."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "The interventions replace model methods only for the diagnostic process; no production mechanics were changed.",
    "The all-animation-clocks variant applies the analogous sourced counters to both mask directions and monitor lowering, but this record measures only monitor-raise counters directly.",
    "The corrected draw prefix is necessary but insufficient for full state equivalence; model/rebuild still differ after update 2047.",
    "No phone interaction or new retail evidence."
  ],
